+
+// The low 24 bits of a VRAM word (PSMZ24 / PSMCT24), its top byte kept: some drivers (Turnip on Adreno 7xx,
+// older Qualcomm drivers) have no 8-bit storage. No atomics: a pixel writes its colour before its depth, so
+// when the two alias, the word read here already holds this invocation's alpha.
+void vram_store_u24(uint word, uint value)
+{
+	vram32.data[word] = bitfieldInsert(vram32.data[word], value, 0, 24);
+}
